The viewBox="0 0 600 300" defines the internal coordinate system of the inline SVG graphic. The four numbers represent: 0 (minimum x, or the left edge), 0 (minimum y, or the top edge), 600 (the width of the drawing canvas), and 300 (the height of the drawing canvas). So the graphic is drawn inside a space that is 600 units wide and 300 units tall — twice as wide as it is high. This gives the two circles (the smaller 14% circle and the larger 29% circle) a comfortable, balanced area to sit side by side with room for their labels. Because these coordinates are relative rather than fixed pixels, the browser can scale the entire graphic proportionally to fit any display width 